Subject: [PATCH 08086/11362] Find a held-out induction metric with headroom:
 exp6018's floor was the choice of primary

exp6018 A/B'd object perception and returned unmeasurable_instrument_floor -- its
pre-registered primary, held-out exact-full-grid transition accuracy, was exactly 0.0
in both arms on all 168 cells, so zero discordant per-game pairs and no test possible.
That blocks every representation change, not just object perception: while the metric
is floored, "the method does not help" and "the measurement had no headroom" are
indistinguishable.

Re-scored the 48 FROZEN best-of-N candidates (results/arc_induce_bestofn_20260731,
2026-07-31) under 13 metrics spanning five granularities, plus a constructed-quality
positive control. CPU only, no GPU, no generation -- the completions, transitions and
proven split were already on disk.

ANSWER: change_fidelity (already shipped, WorldModelVerifier). 39 discordant
within-game candidate pairs across 3 gradable games, against 0 for exact-match on
change-dominated splits. It is the unique metric of the 13 clearing all five criteria:
resolves a corruption ladder monotonically at full [0,1] range, never ranks the
degenerate identity engine above a real engine, penalises spurious writes, separates
real candidates on 2+ games.

Eliminated, with reasons:
* exact-match is ANTI-correlated with dynamics quality here. On ft09 it ranks the
  candidate that predicts nothing ever changes BEST (0.8) while its change_fidelity is
  0.0; all of its variation on the three no-op-dominated games is no-op credit
  (n_changes_correct is 0 for every candidate there). On tu93, whose split is 19/19
  changing, it is 0.0 for all five runnable candidates -- exp6018's floor reproduced
  on an independent corpus.
* The four object metrics this phase ADDED all fail: they rank the identity engine
  above a real-but-bad engine on 3 of 4 games, visible on real candidates (tu93
  object_match_iou puts two engines scoring 0.0 change_fidelity ABOVE one scoring
  0.112). A 64x64 frame's partition is dominated by static background an inert engine
  reproduces perfectly. Says nothing about the object hypothesis; says object-partition
  OVERLAP cannot test it.
* cell_recall is blind to invented writes -- oracle+256 spurious cells still scores 1.0.
* grid agreement spans 0.0002-0.0035 between a perfect and a totally wrong engine.

Corroboration that is exp6018's own and not this phase's: its leak-prompt control put
every held-out transition INTO the prompt and exact-match was still 0.0 in all 28 cells
(its own field reads metric_demonstrably_moves: False), while cell_recall moved in 12.

Also caught: _induce_transitions_k() changed default 8 -> None this morning
(253e1b60ed), so split.py derives a different split than the frozen prompts had. Pinned
to 8 and verified field-by-field against the split proven on 2026-07-31, prompt sha
included. 117 of 117 re-derived values match the frozen run exactly.

Honest limits recorded in the artifact: one arm only, so "floored in BOTH arms" is
answered only for the six channels exp6018 measured in two arms; 5 games of which 3 are
gradable; no causal claim about object perception; the recommended metric is not new,
only newly justified as the primary.

adversarial_verify 0-flagged. No generated code executed in the driver interpreter.

