+ "spearman_reading": "The task's guard is that a graded metric which DISAGREES with exact-match where exact-match works is measuring something else. Applied naively here it would reject the right answer: change_fidelity's pooled within-game-centred Spearman against exact-match is only 0.19. But 3 of the 4 games where exact-match is non-degenerate are the no-op-credit games above, where exact-match is not working -- it is ranking inertness. On tn36, the ONLY game where exact-match is non-degenerate for a dynamics reason, change_fidelity's Spearman against it is exactly 1.0, as is cell_recall's, changed_cell_jaccard's and correct_changed_cells'. So the graded metrics are graded versions of exact-match wherever exact-match means what it claims to, and they diverge from it precisely where it does not.",
